    "standardized_narrative": "At 31 December 2024 the syndicate's prioryears reserves showed material adverse development. Using the gross claims development triangle (UW years 2015-2022) the estimated prioryear strengthening amounts to approximately GBP 194.6m (c.15.1% of opening gross claims outstanding). Key contributors were the westernleased aircraft (Russia) exposures (material uplift), adverse development on the US contractors/general liability (construction defect) book, and a series of catastrophe and large losses (including the Dali bridge collapse and US hurricanes). These movements have driven the decision to keep the 2021 year of account open while uncertainty persists.",
    "raw_causal_phrases": [
      "the syndicate has exposure to the fate of the western leased aircraft in Russia.",
      "The casualty business group experienced deterioration to the prior year reserves as a result of construction defect claims in Florida.",
      "additional gross reserves of GBP 52.7m and GBP 52.3m net of reinsurance were recorded",
      "the specialty business group has been affected by the Dali loss whereby a cargo ship collided with the Francis Scott Key Bridge in Baltimore causing it to collapse on 26 March 2024.",
      "the property business group was affected by Hurricanes Milton and Helene with gross and net losses of GBP 29.0m and GBP 10.0m respectively",
      "the outcome of the most recent modelling ... has been factored in to the latest forecast range for the 2021 year of account",
      "Due to the nature of the circumstances mentioned above, the potential for variation to the booked reserves is considerably greater than the normal level of reserve sensitivity to downside risk"
    ],
